    {
      "id": 2,
      "name": "Rourkela Steel Plant Industrial Project",
      "image": "https://res.cloudinary.com/diml2eds6/image/upload/v1719479878/image_2_s3una3.png",
      "tech stack": [
        "Arduino",
        "Control systems",
        "Signal processing",
        "OpenPLC",
        "Power electronics"
      ],
      "body": "This project aims to develop a modernized industrial motor control system that replaces an outdated Programmable Logic Controller (PLC) with an Arduino-based solution. The system will leverage Arduino's versatility and affordability to precisely control the speed of a motor using a PID (Proportional-Integral-Derivative) control algorithm, while also monitoring and regulating the motor's field current. The unique aspect of this project is the integration of a thyristor stack, which will provide controlled power to the motor based on the Arduino's firing signals. This project will deliver a cost-effective, flexible, and efficient solution for industrial motor control applications.",
